sments or similar fact-finding activities; Experience preparing investigation reports, risk assessments, executive briefings and recommendations for senior decision-makers; Experience integrating information from investigations, intelligence sources, incident reporting and partner information into defensible security-risk assessments; Experience establishing and maintaining relationships with police, intelligence, security or government partners; Experience supporting domestic or international travel-security activities would be considered an asset; Experience developing or improving investigative standards, threat-assessment methodologies, procedures or professional practices would be considered an asset; Knowledge of threat assessment, threat management and security-risk management methodologies; Knowledge of investigative planning, interviewing, evidence assessment and credibility analysis; Knowledge of threats affecting parliamentary institutions, including workplace violence, harassment, insider threats, foreign interference, violent extremism and other emerging security concerns; Knowledge of security, intelligence, law-enforcement and parliamentary partner mandates and authorities; Possess excellent communications skills both orally and in writing in order to prepare and deliver reports and presentations to senior officials including drafting & presenting investigative reports and security briefings; Knowledge of the provisions of security-related acts and regulations, federal and provincial statutes, and criminal and civil law; Possess an in-depth understanding of domestic and international travel risks with experience developing strategies and threat and risk assessments to support the safe realization of travel; Have excellent interpersonal skills with proven experience in developing strong, mutually benefiting relationships with people in the security community; Experience working in a parliamentary, legislative, government, intelligence or security environment would be considered a strong asset. Operational Requirements Willing and able to travel domestically and abroad when required with very little notice; Willing and able to work long and/or irregular hours when required; Will be required to be on call and on standby rotation. Linguistic Requirements English Reading Comprehension: C English Written Expression: B English Oral Interaction: C French Reading Comprehension: C French Written Expression: B French Oral Interaction: C Competencies Integrity Respect Service Action Management Adaptability Communication Developing self and others Teamwork and cooperation Judgement Organizational Needs The Senate of Canada is committed to building and maintaining an inclusive workplace where all employees are provided full and equal access to employment, development and advancement opportunities. Conditions of Employment Candidates must consent to supply personal information and obtain a top security accreditation to be eligible for appointment. Applicants must be legally eligible to work in Canada.
